   "title": "Select fiscal indicators of the Central Government, per cent of GDP"
  },
  "latestPeriod": "2026-27 (financial year)",
  "coverage": "The Centre's deficits, taxes, spending and interest as a share of GDP, 2011-12 to 2026-27, over GDP on the 2011-12 base",
  "note": "RBI, Select fiscal indicators of the Central Government, per cent of GDP (DBIE report 355). Per cent of GDP at current market prices, GDP on the 2011-12 base (the RBI's note on its state-indicators table: 1999-2000 base to 2003-04, 2004-05 base to 2010-11, 2011-12 base from 2011-12; the Centre's and the combined tables divide by the same GDP, checked by their implied denominators). A different GDP base is a different ruler: never joined across bundles. The budget estimate for 2026-27 divides by the budget's own GDP projection. Net tax revenue is net of the states' share and the National Calamity Contingency Fund. Defence excludes pensions and civil spending. Capital receipts exclude the drawdown of cash balances. Stages, from the printed table's own note: accounts to 2024-25, the revised estimate for 2025-26 and the budget estimate for 2026-27, each in its own series (suffix __re and __be), never one line. Cross-checked against the printed table (Innovation Hub export of Handbook report 196): 1253 of 1253 figures match."
 },
